+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "قف وراه. لو طفل، ممكن تحتاج تركع.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "You should perform repeated cycles of 5 back blows followed by 5 abdominal thrusts, until the object comes out or the person becomes unconscious. In pregnant or obese people, chest thrusts should be done instead of abdominal thrusts. To perform back blows: Stand behind the person. For a child, you may have to kneel. Wrap one arm around to support the person's upper body.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "لُفّ ذراع واحدة حواليه عشان تسند جسمه من فوق، وميّله لقدّام لحد ما صدره يبقى موازي للأرض تقريبًا.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "You should perform repeated cycles of 5 back blows followed by 5 abdominal thrusts, until the object comes out or the person becomes unconscious. In pregnant or obese people, chest thrusts should be done instead of abdominal thrusts. To perform back blows: Stand behind the person. For a child, you may have to kneel. Wrap one arm around to support the person's upper body. Lean the person forward until the chest is about parallel to the ground.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "بكعب إيدك التانية اضربه ضربة قوية بين لوحي الكتف، وشوف الحاجة طلعت ولا لأ. كمّل لحد ما تبقى ٥ ضربات.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "To perform back blows: Stand behind the person. For a child, you may have to kneel. Wrap one arm around to support the person's upper body. Lean the person forward until the chest is about parallel to the ground. Use the heel of your other hand to deliver a firm blow between the person's shoulder blades.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "لو ماطلعتش والشخص مش حامل ولا بدين جدًا: لفّ دراعاتك حوالين وسطه، واعمل قبضة فوق سُرّته بشوية وتحت عظمة الصدر.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Continue to give a total of 5 back blows. To perform abdominal thrusts (Heimlich maneuver): Stand behind the person and wrap your arms around the person's waist. For a child, you may have to kneel. Make a fist with one hand. Place the thumb side of your fist just above the person's navel, well below the breastbone.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "No limiting qualifier in this supporting context.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "اعمل ٥ ضغطات سريعة لجوّه ولفوق. كرّر ٥ ضربات و٥ ضغطات لحد ما الجسم يطلع أو يفقد الوعي.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Place the thumb side of your fist just above the person's navel, well below the breastbone. Grasp the fist tightly with your other hand. Make a quick, upward and inward thrust with your fist. Check if the object is dislodged. Continue to give a total of 5 abdominal thrusts. FOR PREGNANT OR OBESE PEOPLE Wrap your arms around the person's CHEST.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[5]",
+          "text": "لو الشخص حامل أو بدين جدًا: اعمل ٥ ضغطات صدر للخلف في نص عظمة الصدر بدل ضغطات البطن.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person cannot speak or is having a hard time breathing, you need to act fast to help the person. You should perform repeated cycles of 5 back blows followed by 5 abdominal thrusts, until the object comes out or the person becomes unconscious. In pregnant or obese people, chest thrusts should be done instead of abdominal thrusts. To perform back blows: Stand behind the person.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[0]",
+          "text": "ماتتدخّلش لو بيسعل بقوة، أو بيقدر يتكلّم، أو بيتنفّس كويس — سيبه يكحّ، بس فضل جنبه.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Anyone who is choking should have a medical exam. Complications can occur not only from the choking, but also from the first aid measures that were taken. DO NOT Avoid making the situation worse by following these tips: Do not interfere if the person is coughing forcefully, is able to speak, or is able to breathe in and out adequately.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[1]",
+          "text": "ماتفتحش بقّه بالعافية عشان تمسك الحاجة وتشدّها وهو واعي — اعمل ضرب ظهر وضغطات بطن.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Avoid making the situation worse by following these tips: Do not interfere if the person is coughing forcefully, is able to speak, or is able to breathe in and out adequately. But, be ready to act right away if the person's symptoms get worse. Do not force open the person's mouth to try to grasp and pull out the object if the person is conscious.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[2]",
+          "text": "ماتسيبهوش لوحده تجري تجيب حاجة.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "When to Contact a Medical Professional Seek medical help right away if you find someone unconscious. When the person is choking: Tell someone to call 911 or the local emergency number while you begin first aid and CPR. If you are alone, shout for help and begin first aid and CPR. After the object is successfully dislodged, the person should see a health care provider because complications can arise.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        }
+      ],
+      "source_qualifiers": [
+        {
+          "id": "scope-conscious-over-one",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_excerpt": "A choking person's airway may be blocked so that not enough oxygen reaches the lungs. Without oxygen, brain damage can occur in as little as 4 minutes. Rapid first aid for choking can save a person's life. This article discusses choking in adults or children over age 1 year who have not lost alertness (are conscious).",
+          "disposition": "Carried by the card identity/snapshot and the separate infant-choking card.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "strong-cough-no-intervention",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person does not do this, look for these danger signs: Inability to speak Difficulty breathing Noisy breathing or high-pitched sounds while inhaling Weak, ineffective coughing Bluish skin color (cyanosis) Loss of consciousness (unresponsiveness) if the blockage is not cleared First Aid First ask, \"Are you choking? Can you speak?\" Do not perform first aid if the person is coughing forcefully and is able to speak. A strong cough can dislodge the object.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by dont[0].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "five-five-cycles-until-out-or-unconscious",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_excerpt": "Encourage the person to keep coughing to dislodge the object. If the person cannot speak or is having a hard time breathing, you need to act fast to help the person. You should perform repeated cycles of 5 back blows followed by 5 abdominal thrusts, until the object comes out or the person becomes unconscious.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[2] and do[4].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "pregnant-obese-chest-thrusts",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person cannot speak or is having a hard time breathing, you need to act fast to help the person. You should perform repeated cycles of 5 back blows followed by 5 abdominal thrusts, until the object comes out or the person becomes unconscious. In pregnant or obese people, chest thrusts should be done instead of abdominal thrusts. To perform back blows: Stand behind the person.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[3] and do[5].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "unconscious-cpr-not-abdominal-thrusts",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_excerpt": "Tell someone to call 911 or the local emergency number. Carefully place the person on a firm and flat surface. Begin CPR . Check for an object in the mouth before giving breaths. Chest compressions may help dislodge the object. Abdominal thrusts are for a conscious choking victim. Chest compressions are for an unconscious choking victim .",
+          "disposition": "Carried by variations and whenWhy.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "post-event-medical-exam",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-adult",
+          "source_excerpt": "Continue giving CPR and checking for the object in the mouth until medical help arrives or the person starts breathing on their own. After removing the object that caused the choking, keep the person still and get medical help. Anyone who is choking should have a medical exam. Complications can occur not only from the choking, but also from the first aid measures that were taken.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by after.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        }
+      ],
