+            "after": "لو نفسه وقف، ابدأ تنفّس إنقاذي أول ما تقدر؛ على اليابسة اعمل الإنعاش القلبي الرئوي لو محتاج."
+          },
+          {
+            "field_path": "do[5].t",
+            "before": "ممكن يكحّ ويتعبه النفس أول ما يرجع يتنفّس — فضل جنبه وطمّنه لحد ما المساعدة توصل.",
+            "after": "لو رجع يتنفّس: طمّنه واطلب مساعدة طبية. لو فيه إصابة واضحة في الراس، ثبّت راسه ورقبته مع جسمه."
+          },
+          {
+            "field_path": "whenWhy.ar",
+            "before": "معظم اللي بيموتوا وهم بينقذوا كانوا غير مدرّبين ونزلوا الميّه — عشان كده «ماتنزلش». والإنعاش فور الخروج بيحافظ على المخ.",
+            "after": "الإنقاذ بالسباحة من غير تدريب ممكن يعرّضك للخطر — عشان كده «ماتنزلش». والإنعاش فور الخروج بيساعد يرجّع التنفّس والدورة الدموية."
+          },
+          {
+            "field_path": "after.ar",
+            "before": "مستشفى إجباري بعد أي غرق حتى لو الشخص بيتنفّس كويس؛ راقب الكحّة وضيق النفس لعدة ساعات.",
+            "after": "لازم كشف طبي بعد أي غرق حتى لو الشخص باين كويس؛ ولو احتاج أي إنعاش لازم يتنقل للمستشفى للتقييم."
+          }
+        ]
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "card_id": "burn",
+      "title": {
+        "ar": "حرق (حرارة أو سوائل مغلية)",
+        "en": "Burn / scald"
+      },
+      "level": 4,
+      "card_sha256": "2bf0bc0290cf8108773349b1e9e4f4875d7417a120673c1c92792c761ff0a6b7",
+      "sources": [
+        {
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000030.htm",
+          "filename": "medlineplus-gov-ency-article-000030-htm-a91249d64f.html",
+          "sha256": "0d66d1418df9bf1104379fabdb398a99ed4f77dd30ecb1decb79c50c551d4d93",
+          "retrieval_date": "2026-08-02",
+          "retrieved_at": "2026-08-02T15:16:12.645Z",
+          "final_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000030.htm",
+          "source_metadata_sha256": "3113ae2e76",
+          "source_metadata_retrieved": "2026-07-10",
+          "licence": "© A.D.A.M./Ebix — مقتبس ومنسوب، مش ملكية عامة"
+        }
+      ],
+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "لو الحرق بسيط والجلد مش مفتوح: سيّب ميّه ساقعة تجري عليه، أو انقعه في ميّه ساقعة — مش بتلج.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "You may have an airway burn if you have: Burns on the head, face, neck, eyebrows, or nose hairs Burned lips and mouth Coughing Difficulty breathing Dark, black-stained mucus Voice changes Wheezing First Aid Before giving first aid, it is important to determine what type of burn the person has. If you are not sure, treat it as a major burn. Serious burns need medical care right away. Call 911 or the local emergency number. MINOR BURNS If the skin is unbroken: Run cool water over the area of the burn or soak it in a cool water bath (not ice water).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "هدّي الشخص وطمّنه.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "MINOR BURNS If the skin is unbroken: Run cool water over the area of the burn or soak it in a cool water bath (not ice water). Keep the area under water for at least 5 to 30 minutes. A clean, cold, wet towel will help reduce pain. Calm and reassure the person. After flushing or soaking the burn, cover it with a dry, sterile bandage or clean dressing.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "بعد ما تغسله أو تنقعه، غطّي الحرق بشاش معقّم ناشف أو قماشة نضيفة.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "MINOR BURNS If the skin is unbroken: Run cool water over the area of the burn or soak it in a cool water bath (not ice water). Keep the area under water for at least 5 to 30 minutes. A clean, cold, wet towel will help reduce pain. Calm and reassure the person. After flushing or soaking the burn, cover it with a dry, sterile bandage or clean dressing. Protect the burn from pressure and friction.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "احمي الحرق من أي ضغط أو احتكاك.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Keep the area under water for at least 5 to 30 minutes. A clean, cold, wet towel will help reduce pain. Calm and reassure the person. After flushing or soaking the burn, cover it with a dry, sterile bandage or clean dressing. Protect the burn from pressure and friction. Over-the-counter ibuprofen or acetaminophen can help relieve pain and swelling.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "لو الهدوم بتولّع: لُفّ الشخص في حاجة تخينة زي بطانية أو معطف صوف أو سجادة عشان تطفّي النار.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Minor burns will often heal without further treatment. Make sure the person is up to date on their tetanus immunization. MAJOR BURNS If someone is on fire, tell the person to stop, drop, and roll. Then, follow these steps: Wrap the person in thick material; such as a wool or cotton coat, rug, or blanket. This helps put out the flames.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[0]",
+          "text": "ماتشيلش الهدوم المحروقة اللي لازقة في الجلد.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Things that should not be done for burns include: Do not apply oil, butter, ice, medicines, cream, oil spray, or any household remedy to a severe burn. Do not breathe, blow, or cough on the burn. Do not disturb blistered or dead skin. Do not remove clothing that is stuck to the skin. Do not give the person anything by mouth if there is a severe burn.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[1]",
+          "text": "ماتغمرش الحرق الشديد في ميّه ساقعة، وماتحطّش عليه زيت ولا زبدة ولا تلج ولا كريم ولا وصفة بيتية.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person does not have a head, neck, back, or leg injury, follow these steps: Lay the person flat Raise the feet about 12 in (30 cm) Cover the person with a coat or blanket Continue to monitor the person's pulse , rate of breathing, and blood pressure until medical help arrives. DO NOT Things that should not be done for burns include: Do not apply oil, butter, ice, medicines, cream, oil spray, or any household remedy to a severe burn. Do not breathe, blow, or cough on the burn.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[2]",
+          "text": "ماتتنفّسش ولا تنفخ ولا تكحّ على الحرق.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:burns",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person does not have a head, neck, back, or leg injury, follow these steps: Lay the person flat Raise the feet about 12 in (30 cm) Cover the person with a coat or blanket Continue to monitor the person's pulse , rate of breathing, and blood pressure until medical help arrives. DO NOT Things that should not be done for burns include: Do not apply oil, butter, ice, medicines, cream, oil spray, or any household remedy to a severe burn. Do not breathe, blow, or cough on the burn. Do not disturb blistered or dead skin.",
