+          "source_excerpt": "You may have an airway burn if you have: Burns on the head, face, neck, eyebrows, or nose hairs Burned lips and mouth Coughing Difficulty breathing Dark, black-stained mucus Voice changes Wheezing First Aid Before giving first aid, it is important to determine what type of burn the person has. If you are not sure, treat it as a major burn. Serious burns need medical care right away. Call 911 or the local emergency number. MINOR BURNS If the skin is unbroken: Run cool water over the area of the burn or soak it in a cool water bath (not ice water).",
