+    {
+      "card_id": "infant-choking",
+      "title": {
+        "ar": "رضيع بيختنق (أقل من سنة)",
+        "en": "Infant choking (under 1)"
+      },
+      "level": 5,
+      "card_sha256": "dd556063d757a14678561209e8b7936c432a9c745ca25cbc26e3a38b8d88b23f",
+      "sources": [
+        {
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000048.htm",
+          "filename": "medlineplus-gov-ency-article-000048-htm-214b4c7031.html",
+          "sha256": "88a94dfe08c3e14b9ef83bd5015722ad77554c3544ab5308b4eb7df5886f512e",
+          "retrieval_date": "2026-08-02",
+          "retrieved_at": "2026-08-02T15:16:12.994Z",
+          "final_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000048.htm",
+          "source_metadata_sha256": "a7c34e47b5",
+          "source_metadata_retrieved": "2026-07-10",
+          "licence": "© A.D.A.M./Ebix — مقتبس ومنسوب، مش ملكية عامة"
+        }
+      ],
+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "نيّمه على بطنه على ساعدك، وسند ساعدك على فخذك أو حِضنك، وامسك صدره في إيدك وفكّه بصوابعك، وخلّي راسه مايلة لتحت أوطى من مستوى جسمه.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Symptoms The danger signs of choking are: Bluish skin color (cyanosis) Difficulty breathing -- ribs and chest pull inward Loss of consciousness (unresponsiveness) if the blockage is not cleared Inability to cry or make much sound Weak, ineffective coughing Soft or high-pitched sounds while inhaling First Aid Do not perform these steps if the infant is coughing hard or has a strong cry. Strong coughs and cries can help push the object out of the airway. If the infant is not coughing forcefully or does not have a strong cry, follow these steps: Lay the infant face down, along your forearm. Use your thigh or lap for support.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "اديله لحد ٥ ضربات سريعة وقوية بين لوحي كتفه براحة إيدك التانية.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the infant is not coughing forcefully or does not have a strong cry, follow these steps: Lay the infant face down, along your forearm. Use your thigh or lap for support. Hold the infant's chest in your hand and the jaw with your fingers. Point the infant's head downward, lower than the body. Give up to 5 quick, forceful blows between the infant's shoulder blades (back blows).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "اقلبه على ضهره، وسنده على فخذك أو حِضنك، وسند راسه.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Give up to 5 quick, forceful blows between the infant's shoulder blades (back blows). Use the palm of your free hand. If the object does not come out of the airway after 5 blows: Turn the infant face-up. Use your thigh or lap for support. Support the head. Place the heel of one hand on the middle of the breastbone just below the nipples.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "حُط كعب إيد واحدة في نص عظمة الصدر تحت الحلمتين بشوية، واعمل لحد ٥ ضغطات صدر لتحت.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Give up to 5 quick, forceful blows between the infant's shoulder blades (back blows). Use the palm of your free hand. If the object does not come out of the airway after 5 blows: Turn the infant face-up. Use your thigh or lap for support. Support the head. Place the heel of one hand on the middle of the breastbone just below the nipples. Give up to 5 quick chest thrusts down.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "لو شايف الحاجة اللي قافلة مجرى الهوا، حاول تطلّعها بصباعك — بس بشرط تكون شايفها.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Place the heel of one hand on the middle of the breastbone just below the nipples. Give up to 5 quick chest thrusts down. If you can see the object blocking the airway, try to remove it with your finger. Only try to remove an object if you can see it. Continue 5 back blows followed by 5 chest thrusts until the object is dislodged or the infant loses alertness (becomes unconscious).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[5]",
+          "text": "كمّل ٥ ضرب ظهر وبعدها ٥ ضغطات صدر لحد ما الحاجة تطلع أو الرضيع يغيب عن الوعي.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Place the heel of one hand on the middle of the breastbone just below the nipples. Give up to 5 quick chest thrusts down. If you can see the object blocking the airway, try to remove it with your finger. Only try to remove an object if you can see it. Continue 5 back blows followed by 5 chest thrusts until the object is dislodged or the infant loses alertness (becomes unconscious).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[0]",
+          "text": "ماتعملش إسعاف اختناق لو الرضيع بيسعل بقوة، أو عياطه قوي، أو بيتنفّس كفاية.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Anyone who is choking should have a medical exam. Complications can occur not only from the choking, but also from the first aid measures that were taken. DO NOT Avoid making the situation worse by following these tips: Do not perform choking first aid if the infant is coughing forcefully, has a strong cry, or is breathing enough.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[1]",
+          "text": "ماتحاولش تمسك الحاجة وتشدّها وهو صاحي وواعي.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Avoid making the situation worse by following these tips: Do not perform choking first aid if the infant is coughing forcefully, has a strong cry, or is breathing enough. However, be ready to act if the symptoms get worse. Do not try to grasp and pull out the object if the infant is alert (conscious).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[2]",
+          "text": "ماتعملش ضرب ظهر وضغطات صدر لو الرضيع بطّل يتنفّس لسبب تاني، زي الربو أو عدوى أو تورّم.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Avoid making the situation worse by following these tips: Do not perform choking first aid if the infant is coughing forcefully, has a strong cry, or is breathing enough. However, be ready to act if the symptoms get worse. Do not try to grasp and pull out the object if the infant is alert (conscious). Do not do back blows and chest thrusts if the infant stops breathing for other reasons, such as asthma, infection, swelling, or a blow to the head.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        }
+      ],
+      "source_qualifiers": [
+        {
+          "id": "scope-under-one",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "A choking infant's airway may be blocked so that not enough oxygen reaches the lungs. Without oxygen, brain damage can occur in as little as 4 minutes. Rapid first aid for choking can save an infant's life. This article discusses choking in infants under 1 year of age. Causes Choking in infants is usually caused by breathing in a small object that the baby has placed in their mouth, such as a button, coin, balloon, toy part, or watch battery.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by title and card ID.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "strong-cough-or-cry",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "Symptoms The danger signs of choking are: Bluish skin color (cyanosis) Difficulty breathing -- ribs and chest pull inward Loss of consciousness (unresponsiveness) if the blockage is not cleared Inability to cry or make much sound Weak, ineffective coughing Soft or high-pitched sounds while inhaling First Aid Do not perform these steps if the infant is coughing hard or has a strong cry. Strong coughs and cries can help push the object out of the airway.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by dont[0].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "visible-object-only",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "Place the heel of one hand on the middle of the breastbone just below the nipples. Give up to 5 quick chest thrusts down. If you can see the object blocking the airway, try to remove it with your finger. Only try to remove an object if you can see it. Continue 5 back blows followed by 5 chest thrusts until the object is dislodged or the infant loses alertness (becomes unconscious).",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[4].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "cycles-until-object-or-unconscious",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "If you can see the object blocking the airway, try to remove it with your finger. Only try to remove an object if you can see it. Continue 5 back blows followed by 5 chest thrusts until the object is dislodged or the infant loses alertness (becomes unconscious).",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[5].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "alone-two-minutes-cpr",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "Give infant CPR . Check for an object in the mouth before giving breaths. If you are alone, leave the infant to call 911 or the local emergency number, or carry the infant with you, only after you have performed 2 minutes of CPR.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by variations.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "other-cause-use-cpr",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "Do not try to grasp and pull out the object if the infant is alert (conscious). Do not do back blows and chest thrusts if the infant stops breathing for other reasons, such as asthma, infection, swelling, or a blow to the head. Do give the infant CPR in these cases. When to Contact a Medical Professional If an infant is choking: Tell someone to call 911 or the local emergency number while you begin first aid.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by dont[2] together with variations.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "provider-after-success",
+          "source_id": "mlp:choking-infant",
+          "source_excerpt": "When to Contact a Medical Professional If an infant is choking: Tell someone to call 911 or the local emergency number while you begin first aid. If you are alone, shout for help and begin first aid. Always call your child's health care provider after a child has been choking, even if you successfully remove the object from the airway and the infant seems fine.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by after.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        }
+      ],
+      "overall_verdict": "PASS",
+      "reviewer_note": "Human full-card review against the complete fetched First Aid, DO NOT, and escalation context; no heuristic was used to award PASS.",
+      "remediation": {
+        "changed": false,
+        "before_card_sha256": "dd556063d757a14678561209e8b7936c432a9c745ca25cbc26e3a38b8d88b23f",
+        "after_card_sha256": "dd556063d757a14678561209e8b7936c432a9c745ca25cbc26e3a38b8d88b23f",
+        "modified_fields": []
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "card_id": "heat-stroke",
+      "title": {
+        "ar": "إجهاد حراري وضربة شمس",
+        "en": "Heat exhaustion & heat stroke"
+      },
+      "level": 4,
+      "card_sha256": "d19a7644dac827dc518d989eb3a33a7dce0c877f5a19545c4eec6b7f4a46d5cc",
+      "sources": [
+        {
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000056.htm",
+          "filename": "medlineplus-gov-ency-article-000056-htm-9e0c1c93c6.html",
+          "sha256": "240e6394f7aa8200fd68ba4a1df4deac90df78b8ea396676706ebf7d2d311bf0",
+          "retrieval_date": "2026-08-02",
+          "retrieved_at": "2026-08-02T15:16:13.041Z",
+          "final_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000056.htm",
+          "source_metadata_sha256": "b04003bdbe",
+          "source_metadata_retrieved": "2026-07-10",
+          "licence": "© A.D.A.M./Ebix — مقتبس ومنسوب، مش ملكية عامة"
+        }
+      ],
+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "نيّمه في مكان بارد، وارفع رجليه حوالي ٣٠ سنتيمتر.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "The symptoms of heatstroke include those of heat exhaustion in combination with very high body temperature and significant neurologic symptoms (call 911 or the local emergency number right away): Fever - temperature above 104°F (40°C) Confusion (altered level of consciousness) Irrational behavior Seizures Slurred speech Extreme lethargy Unconsciousness (loss of responsiveness) First Aid If you think a person may have heat illness or emergency: Have the person lie down in a cool place. Raise the person's feet about 12 inches (30 centimeters).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "حُط على جلده قماش مبلول ساقع (أو ميّه ساقعة على طول)، واستخدم مروحة عشان تنزّل حرارة جسمه.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "The symptoms of heatstroke include those of heat exhaustion in combination with very high body temperature and significant neurologic symptoms (call 911 or the local emergency number right away): Fever - temperature above 104°F (40°C) Confusion (altered level of consciousness) Irrational behavior Seizures Slurred speech Extreme lethargy Unconsciousness (loss of responsiveness) First Aid If you think a person may have heat illness or emergency: Have the person lie down in a cool place. Raise the person's feet about 12 inches (30 centimeters). Apply cool, wet cloths (or cool water directly) to the person's skin and use a fan to lower body temperature.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "لو واعي، ادّيله مشروب رياضي، أو ميّه ساقعة عادية، يرشف منها بالراحة.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Raise the person's feet about 12 inches (30 centimeters). Apply cool, wet cloths (or cool water directly) to the person's skin and use a fan to lower body temperature. Place cold compresses on the person's neck, groin, and armpits. If alert, give the person a beverage to sip (such as a sports drink), or make a salted drink by adding a teaspoon (6 grams) of salt per quart (1 liter) of water.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "لو عنده تقلّصات عضلية: ادّيله المشروبات دي، ودلّك العضلة برفق بس بثبات لحد ما التقلّص يروح.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "If alert, give the person a beverage to sip (such as a sports drink), or make a salted drink by adding a teaspoon (6 grams) of salt per quart (1 liter) of water. Give a half cup (120 milliliters) every 15 minutes. Cool water will do if salt beverages are not available. For muscle cramps, give beverages as noted above and massage affected muscles gently, but firmly, until they relax.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "لو ظهرت عليه علامات صدمة (شفايف وأظافر بتزرقّ، ووعي بيقلّ) أو بدأ يتشنّج: دي طوارئ.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Give a half cup (120 milliliters) every 15 minutes. Cool water will do if salt beverages are not available. For muscle cramps, give beverages as noted above and massage affected muscles gently, but firmly, until they relax. If the person shows signs of shock ( bluish lips and fingernails and decreased alertness ), starts having seizures, or loses consciousness, call 911 or the local emergency number and give first aid as needed.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[0]",
+          "text": "ماتديهوش أدوية الحرارة زي الأسبرين أو الباراسيتامول.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person shows signs of shock ( bluish lips and fingernails and decreased alertness ), starts having seizures, or loses consciousness, call 911 or the local emergency number and give first aid as needed. DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not give the person medicines that are used to treat fever (such as aspirin or acetaminophen).",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[1]",
+          "text": "ماتديهوش أقراص ملح.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person shows signs of shock ( bluish lips and fingernails and decreased alertness ), starts having seizures, or loses consciousness, call 911 or the local emergency number and give first aid as needed. DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not give the person medicines that are used to treat fever (such as aspirin or acetaminophen). They will not help, and they may be harmful. Do not give the person salt tablets. Do not give the person liquids that contain alcohol or caffeine.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[2]",
+          "text": "ماتديهوش مشروبات فيها كحول أو كافيين — بتصعّب على جسمه إنه يتحكّم في حرارته.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not give the person medicines that are used to treat fever (such as aspirin or acetaminophen). They will not help, and they may be harmful. Do not give the person salt tablets. Do not give the person liquids that contain alcohol or caffeine. They will make it harder for the body to control its internal temperature.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "No limiting qualifier in this supporting context.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[3]",
+          "text": "ماتمسحش جلده بالكحول.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "They will not help, and they may be harmful. Do not give the person salt tablets. Do not give the person liquids that contain alcohol or caffeine. They will make it harder for the body to control its internal temperature. Do not use alcohol rubs on the person's skin. Do not give the person anything by mouth (not even salted drinks) if the person is vomiting or unconscious.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[4]",
+          "text": "ماتديهوش أي حاجة بالبق — ولا حتى مشروب بملح — لو بيرجّع أو فاقد الوعي.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Do not give the person liquids that contain alcohol or caffeine. They will make it harder for the body to control its internal temperature. Do not use alcohol rubs on the person's skin. Do not give the person anything by mouth (not even salted drinks) if the person is vomiting or unconscious. When to Contact a Medical Professional Call 911 or the local emergency number if: The person loses consciousness at any time.",
