+          "source_id": "mlp:heat",
+          "source_excerpt": "If alert, give the person a beverage to sip (such as a sports drink), or make a salted drink by adding a teaspoon (6 grams) of salt per quart (1 liter) of water. Give a half cup (120 milliliters) every 15 minutes. Cool water will do if salt beverages are not available. For muscle cramps, give beverages as noted above and massage affected muscles gently, but firmly, until they relax.",
