+    {
+      "card_id": "head-injury",
+      "title": {
+        "ar": "إصابة في الراس",
+        "en": "Head injury"
+      },
+      "level": 4,
+      "card_sha256": "9d4ce4e953532f7fbcb39e9737ca0c3335d0ba76615fb6cae778ded879ebfaa9",
+      "sources": [
+        {
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000028.htm",
+          "filename": "medlineplus-gov-ency-article-000028-htm-6f5c25540f.html",
+          "sha256": "2c57d6a6580183b072ea1116209e3a5ba50f744f7a40dc9ebdea0cb1696af805",
+          "retrieval_date": "2026-08-02",
+          "retrieved_at": "2026-08-02T15:16:12.613Z",
+          "final_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000028.htm",
+          "source_metadata_sha256": "1c5457c4a4",
+          "source_metadata_retrieved": null,
+          "licence": null
+        }
+      ],
+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "اطمّن على مجرى الهوا والتنفّس والدورة الدموية عند المصاب. ولو محتاج، ابدأ تنفّس صناعي وإنعاش قلبي (CPR).",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Get medical help right away if the person: Becomes very sleepy Behaves abnormally, or has speech that does not make sense Develops a severe headache or stiff neck Has a seizure Has pupils (the dark central part of the eye) of unequal sizes Is unable to move all or part of an arm or leg Loses consciousness, even briefly Vomits more than once Then take the following steps: Check the person's airway, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin rescue breathing and CPR .",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "لو نفَسه ونبضه طبيعيين بس مش واعي، اعتبر إن فيه إصابة في العمود الفقري. ثبّت الراس والرقبة بإنك تحط إيديك على جنبي راسه، وخليها في خط واحد مع الظهر ومتسيبهاش تتحرك، واستنى الإسعاف.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Get medical help right away if the person: Becomes very sleepy Behaves abnormally, or has speech that does not make sense Develops a severe headache or stiff neck Has a seizure Has pupils (the dark central part of the eye) of unequal sizes Is unable to move all or part of an arm or leg Loses consciousness, even briefly Vomits more than once Then take the following steps: Check the person's airway, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin rescue breathing and CPR . If the person's breathing and heart rate are normal, but the person is unconscious , treat as if there is a spinal injury . Stabilize the head and neck by placing your hands on both sides of the person's head. Keep the head in line with the spine and prevent movement. Wait for medical help.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "وقّف أي نزيف بإنك تضغط بقوة بقماشة نضيفة على الجرح، إلا لو شاكك إن فيه كسر في الجمجمة. ولو الإصابة خطيرة، خلي بالك ماتحرّكش راسه. ولو الدم نشّ في القماشة، ماتشيلهاش — حط قماشة تانية فوق الأولى.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person's breathing and heart rate are normal, but the person is unconscious , treat as if there is a spinal injury . Stabilize the head and neck by placing your hands on both sides of the person's head. Keep the head in line with the spine and prevent movement. Wait for medical help. Stop any bleeding by firmly pressing a clean cloth on the wound, unless you suspect a skull fracture. If the injury is serious, be careful not to move the person's head. If blood soaks through the cloth, do not remove it. Place another cloth over the first one. If you suspect a skull fracture, do not apply direct pressure to the bleeding site, and do not remove any debris from the wound.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "لو شاكك إن فيه كسر في الجمجمة، ماتضغطش على مكان النزيف على طول، وماتشيلش أي حاجة واقعة جوه الجرح. غطّي الجرح بشاش معقّم.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Stop any bleeding by firmly pressing a clean cloth on the wound, unless you suspect a skull fracture. If the injury is serious, be careful not to move the person's head. If blood soaks through the cloth, do not remove it. Place another cloth over the first one. If you suspect a skull fracture, do not apply direct pressure to the bleeding site, and do not remove any debris from the wound. Cover the wound with sterile gauze dressing. If the person is vomiting or about to vomit, to prevent choking , roll the person's head, neck, and body as one unit while stabilizing the head and neck onto their side.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "حط كمّادات تلج على الأماكن المتورّمة (لفّ التلج في فوطة عشان ماياخدش على الجلد على طول).",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "This still protects the spine, which you must always assume is injured in the case of a head injury. Children often vomit once after a head injury. This may not be a problem, but contact your health care provider for further guidance. Apply ice packs to swollen areas (cover ice in a towel so it does not directly touch the skin). DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[5]",
+          "text": "لو بيرجّع، ثبّت الراس والرقبة ولفّ الراس والرقبة والجسم كوحدة واحدة على جنبه عشان مايشرقش.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Place another cloth over the first one. If you suspect a skull fracture, do not apply direct pressure to the bleeding site, and do not remove any debris from the wound. Cover the wound with sterile gauze dressing. If the person is vomiting or about to vomit, to prevent choking , roll the person's head, neck, and body as one unit while stabilizing the head and neck onto their side.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[0]",
+          "text": "ماتحرّكش المصاب إلا للضرورة القصوى.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Apply ice packs to swollen areas (cover ice in a towel so it does not directly touch the skin). DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot. Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound. Do not move the person unless absolutely necessary. Do not shake the person if they seem dazed.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[1]",
+          "text": "ماتشيلش أي حاجة غارزة أو نافرة من الجرح.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Apply ice packs to swollen areas (cover ice in a towel so it does not directly touch the skin). DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot. Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound. Do not move the person unless absolutely necessary.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[2]",
+          "text": "ماتهزّش المصاب لو باين عليه إنه مش مركّز أو سرحان.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot. Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound. Do not move the person unless absolutely necessary. Do not shake the person if they seem dazed. Do not remove a helmet if you suspect a serious head injury.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[3]",
+          "text": "ماتشيلش الخوذة لو شاكك إن الإصابة في الراس خطيرة.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot. Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound. Do not move the person unless absolutely necessary. Do not shake the person if they seem dazed. Do not remove a helmet if you suspect a serious head injury. Do not pick up a fallen child with any sign of head injury.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[4]",
+          "text": "ماتغسلش جرح الراس لو كان عميق أو بينزف كتير.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "This may not be a problem, but contact your health care provider for further guidance. Apply ice packs to swollen areas (cover ice in a towel so it does not directly touch the skin). DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot. Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "No limiting qualifier in this supporting context.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[5]",
+          "text": "ماتشيلش طفل وقع ولسّه عليه أي علامة إصابة في الراس.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound. Do not move the person unless absolutely necessary. Do not shake the person if they seem dazed. Do not remove a helmet if you suspect a serious head injury. Do not pick up a fallen child with any sign of head injury. Do not drink alcohol or use street drugs within 48 hours of a serious head injury.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        }
+      ],
+      "source_qualifiers": [
+        {
+          "id": "moderate-severe-emergency",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "A concussion is a type of traumatic brain injury. Symptoms of a concussion can range from mild to severe. First Aid Learning to recognize a serious head injury and give basic first aid can save someone's life. For a moderate to severe head injury, call 911 or the local emergency number right away. Get medical help right away if the person: Becomes very sleepy Behaves abnormally, or has speech that does not make sense Develops a severe headache or stiff neck Has a seizure Has pupils (the dark central part of the eye) of unequal sizes Is unable to move all or part of an arm or leg Loses consciousness, even briefly Vomits more than once Then take the following steps: Check the person's airway, breathing, and circulation.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by redFlags and whoToCall.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "unconscious-spinal-treatment",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "Get medical help right away if the person: Becomes very sleepy Behaves abnormally, or has speech that does not make sense Develops a severe headache or stiff neck Has a seizure Has pupils (the dark central part of the eye) of unequal sizes Is unable to move all or part of an arm or leg Loses consciousness, even briefly Vomits more than once Then take the following steps: Check the person's airway, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin rescue breathing and CPR . If the person's breathing and heart rate are normal, but the person is unconscious , treat as if there is a spinal injury .",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[1], including treatment as a spinal injury when unconscious.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "skull-fracture-pressure-exception",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "Stabilize the head and neck by placing your hands on both sides of the person's head. Keep the head in line with the spine and prevent movement. Wait for medical help. Stop any bleeding by firmly pressing a clean cloth on the wound, unless you suspect a skull fracture.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[2] and do[3].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "vomiting-log-roll",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "If you suspect a skull fracture, do not apply direct pressure to the bleeding site, and do not remove any debris from the wound. Cover the wound with sterile gauze dressing. If the person is vomiting or about to vomit, to prevent choking , roll the person's head, neck, and body as one unit while stabilizing the head and neck onto their side.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by do[5] with head/neck/body as one unit.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "child-single-vomit-boundary",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person is vomiting or about to vomit, to prevent choking , roll the person's head, neck, and body as one unit while stabilizing the head and neck onto their side. This still protects the spine, which you must always assume is injured in the case of a head injury. Children often vomit once after a head injury. This may not be a problem, but contact your health care provider for further guidance.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by redFlags, which escalates vomiting more than once, and aftercare monitoring.",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "deep-bleeding-wound-no-wash",
+          "source_id": "mlp:head-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "This may not be a problem, but contact your health care provider for further guidance. Apply ice packs to swollen areas (cover ice in a towel so it does not directly touch the skin). DO NOT Follow these precautions: Do not wash a head wound that is deep or bleeding a lot. Do not remove any object sticking out of a wound.",
+          "disposition": "Carried by dont[4].",
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        }
+      ],
+      "overall_verdict": "PASS",
+      "reviewer_note": "Human full-card review against the complete fetched First Aid, DO NOT, and escalation context; no heuristic was used to award PASS.",
+      "remediation": {
+        "changed": true,
+        "before_card_sha256": "68f715d3072adb10739ec381910aafd86abf0c297b37cdbb35b4a2c66081d603",
