+    {
+      "card_id": "dislocation",
+      "title": {
+        "ar": "خلع في المفصل",
+        "en": "Dislocation"
+      },
+      "level": 4,
+      "card_sha256": "c3e498b7b4c3568277cf5362166c084eac05646922f7f039c4c3365cf5cb0f2c",
+      "sources": [
+        {
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000014.htm",
+          "filename": "medlineplus-gov-ency-article-000014-htm-9a52c9aa76.html",
+          "sha256": "51749ea3de8e5aa6b3ff64e79061a15242b5f782a39153cf8ca73abdd0b5c020",
+          "retrieval_date": "2026-08-02",
+          "retrieved_at": "2026-08-02T15:16:12.609Z",
+          "final_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000014.htm",
+          "source_metadata_sha256": "51749ea3de",
+          "source_metadata_retrieved": null,
+          "licence": null
+        }
+      ],
+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "اتصل بالطوارئ قبل ما تبدأ تساعد حد ممكن يكون عنده خلع، خصوصًا لو الحادث اللي سبّب الإصابة ممكن يهدد حياته.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Symptoms A dislocated joint may be: Accompanied by numbness or tingling at the joint or beyond it Very painful, especially if you try to use the joint or put weight on it Limited in movement Swollen or bruised Visibly out of place, discolored, or misshapen Nursemaid's elbow , or pulled elbow, is a partial dislocation that is common in toddlers. The main symptom is pain so that the child doesn't want to use the arm. This dislocation can be easily treated in your provider's office. First Aid First aid steps to take: Call 911 or the local emergency number before you begin treating someone who may have a dislocation, especially if the accident that caused the injury may be life threatening. If the person has a serious injury, check their airway, breathing, and circulation.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "لو الإصابة خطيرة، اتأكد من مجرى الهوا والتنفس والدورة الدموية. ولو محتاج، ابدأ إنعاش قلبي رئوي أو سيطر على النزيف.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "First Aid First aid steps to take: Call 911 or the local emergency number before you begin treating someone who may have a dislocation, especially if the accident that caused the injury may be life threatening. If the person has a serious injury, check their airway, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin CPR , or bleeding control.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "لو الجلد مفتوح، امنع العدوى: ماتنفخش على الجرح. اشطف المكان بالراحة بميّه نضيفة عشان تشيل التراب اللي شايفه، بس ماتفركش ولا تنكش فيه. غطّيه بشاش معقم قبل ما تثبّت المفصل، وماتحاولش ترجع العضمة مكانها إلا لو إنت متخصص عظام.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "If the person has a serious injury, check their airway, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin CPR , or bleeding control. Do not move the person if you think that their head, back, or leg has been injured. Keep the person calm and still. If the skin is broken, take steps to prevent infection. Do not blow on the wound. Rinse the area gently with clean water to remove any dirt you can see, but do not scrub or probe. Cover the area with sterile dressings before immobilizing the injured joint. Do not attempt to put the bone back in place unless you are a bone specialist. Apply a splint or sling to the injured joint in the position in which you found it.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "ثبّت المفصل المصاب بجبيرة أو حمّالة في نفس الوضع اللي لقيته عليه. ماتحرّكش المفصل، وثبّت كمان المنطقة اللي فوق الإصابة واللي تحتها.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Rinse the area gently with clean water to remove any dirt you can see, but do not scrub or probe. Cover the area with sterile dressings before immobilizing the injured joint. Do not attempt to put the bone back in place unless you are a bone specialist. Apply a splint or sling to the injured joint in the position in which you found it. Do not move the joint. Also immobilize the area above and below the injured area. Check blood circulation around the injury by pressing firmly on the skin in the affected area.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "افحص الدورة الدموية حوالين الإصابة بإنك تضغط جامد على الجلد في المكان المصاب. المفروض يبيضّ وبعد ما تبطل ضغط يرجع لونه خلال ثانيتين تقريبًا. ماتعملش الخطوة دي لو الجلد مفتوح عشان تقلل خطر العدوى.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Do not attempt to put the bone back in place unless you are a bone specialist. Apply a splint or sling to the injured joint in the position in which you found it. Do not move the joint. Also immobilize the area above and below the injured area. Check blood circulation around the injury by pressing firmly on the skin in the affected area. It should turn white, then regain color within a couple of seconds after you stop pressing on it. To reduce the risk for developing infection, do not do this step if the skin is broken. Apply ice packs to ease pain and swelling, but do not put ice directly on the skin.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
