+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[0]",
+          "text": "ماتحرّكش الشخص لو شاكك إن راسه أو ضهره أو رجله اتصابت. خليه هادي وثابت.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "First Aid First aid steps to take: Call 911 or the local emergency number before you begin treating someone who may have a dislocation, especially if the accident that caused the injury may be life threatening. If the person has a serious injury, check their airway, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin CPR , or bleeding control. Do not move the person if you think that their head, back, or leg has been injured. Keep the person calm and still. If the skin is broken, take steps to prevent infection.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[1]",
+          "text": "ماتحرّكش الشخص إلا بعد ما الإصابة تتثبّت بالكامل.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Unless there is a head, leg, or back injury, lay the victim flat, elevate their feet about 12 inches (in) or 30 centimeters (cm), and cover the person with a coat or blanket. DO NOT Do not move the person unless the injury has been completely immobilized. Do not move a person with an injured hip, pelvis, or upper leg unless it is absolutely necessary.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[2]",
+          "text": "ماتحاولش تفرد عضمة أو مفصل شكله متغيّر، ولا تحاول تغيّر وضعه.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Do not move a person with an injured hip, pelvis, or upper leg unless it is absolutely necessary. If you are the only rescuer and the person must be moved, drag them by their clothing. Do not attempt to straighten a misshapen bone or joint or try to change its position. Do not test a misshapen bone or joint for loss of function.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[3]",
+          "text": "ماتختبرش العضمة أو المفصل اللي شكله متغيّر عشان تشوف فقد وظيفته ولا لأ.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "Do not move a person with an injured hip, pelvis, or upper leg unless it is absolutely necessary. If you are the only rescuer and the person must be moved, drag them by their clothing. Do not attempt to straighten a misshapen bone or joint or try to change its position. Do not test a misshapen bone or joint for loss of function. Do not give the person anything by mouth.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "dont[4]",
+          "text": "ماتديش الشخص أي حاجة عن طريق البق.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:dislocation",
+          "source_context_section": "DO NOT / safety context",
+          "source_excerpt": "If you are the only rescuer and the person must be moved, drag them by their clothing. Do not attempt to straighten a misshapen bone or joint or try to change its position. Do not test a misshapen bone or joint for loss of function. Do not give the person anything by mouth. When to Contact a Medical Professional Call 911 or the local emergency number right away if the person has any of the following: A bone projecting through the skin A known or suspected dislocation or broken bone An area below the injured joint that is pale, cold, clammy, or blue Severe bleeding Signs of infection, such as warmth or redness at the injured site, pus, or a fever Prevention To help prevent injuries in children: Create a safe environment around your home.",
