+        {
+          "id": "straddle-escalation",
+          "source_id": "mlp:genital-injury",
+          "source_excerpt": "If you think the injury was the result of assault or abuse, DO NOT let the person change clothes or take a bath or shower. Seek medical help right away. When to Contact a Medical Professional A straddle injury is damage to the testicle or urinary tract. Get medical help right away if there is: A lot of swelling or bruising Blood in the urine Difficulty urinating Seek medical help right away if there is a genital injury and: Pain, bleeding, or swelling A concern about sexual abuse Problems urinating Blood in the urine Open wound Large amount of swelling or bruising of the genitals or surrounding areas Prevention Teach safety to young children and create a safe environment for them.",
