+    {
+      "card_id": "skull-fracture",
+      "title": {
+        "ar": "كسر في الجمجمة",
+        "en": "Skull fracture"
+      },
+      "level": 5,
+      "card_sha256": "0175f6fbac0dc443de8b40c5884934cdfac2b9a92cbdfed70b5816ca4067d3e8",
+      "sources": [
+        {
+          "source_id": "mlp:skull-fracture",
+          "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000060.htm",
+          "filename": "medlineplus-gov-ency-article-000060-htm-dfe577a34e.html",
+          "sha256": "ca7e884edba7e0f28a363a8d7050f46ab99685dd520288de0d647ea2bdfb5713",
+          "retrieval_date": "2026-08-02",
+          "retrieved_at": "2026-08-02T15:16:13.088Z",
+          "final_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000060.htm",
+          "source_metadata_sha256": "3ef322663e",
+          "source_metadata_retrieved": null,
+          "licence": null
+        }
+      ],
+      "actionable_lines": [
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[0]",
+          "text": "افحص مجرى الهوا والنفس والدورة الدموية. لو ضروري، ابدأ تنفّس إنقاذي وإنعاش قلبي رئوي.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:skull-fracture",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Causes Causes of skull fracture can include: Head trauma Falls, automobile accidents, physical assault, and sports Symptoms Symptoms may include: Bleeding from the wound, ears, nose, or around the eyes Bruising behind the ears or under the eyes Changes in pupils ( sizes unequal or not reactive to light) Confusion Convulsions ( seizures ) Difficulties with balance Drainage of clear or bloody fluid from the ears or nose Drowsiness Headache Loss of consciousness (unresponsiveness) Nausea and vomiting Restlessness , irritability Slurred speech Stiff neck Swelling Visual disturbances In some cases, the only symptom may be a bump on the head. A bump or bruise may take up to 24 hours to develop. First Aid Take the following steps if you think someone has a skull fracture: Check the airways, breathing, and circulation. If necessary, begin rescue breathing and CPR .",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[1]",
+          "text": "لو لازم تحرّكه، ثبّت راسه ورقبته. حُط إيديك على الناحيتين من راسه وتحت كتافه، وماتخلّيش راسه تنحني لقدّام أو لورا، ولا تلف أو تدور.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:skull-fracture",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "If necessary, begin rescue breathing and CPR . Avoid moving the person (unless absolutely necessary) until medical help arrives. Have someone call 911 or the local emergency number for medical assistance. If the person must be moved, take care to stabilize the head and neck. Place your hands on both sides of the head and under the shoulders. Do not allow the head to bend forward or backward, or to twist or turn. Carefully check the site of injury, but do not probe in or around the site with a foreign object.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[2]",
+          "text": "لو فيه نزيف، اضغط بقوة بقماشة نضيفة على مساحة واسعة عشان تقلّل فقدان الدم، بس ماتضغطش مباشرة على مكان شاكك إنه كسر في الجمجمة.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:skull-fracture",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "Carefully check the site of injury, but do not probe in or around the site with a foreign object. It can be hard to know if the skull is fractured or depressed (dented in) at the site of injury. If there is bleeding, apply firm pressure with a clean cloth over a broad area to control blood loss, but do not apply pressure directly onto a suspected skull fracture. If blood soaks through, do not remove the original cloth.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[3]",
+          "text": "لو الدم شرّب القماشة، ماتشيلهاش. حُط قماش أكتر فوقها وكمّل ضغط.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:skull-fracture",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
+          "source_excerpt": "It can be hard to know if the skull is fractured or depressed (dented in) at the site of injury. If there is bleeding, apply firm pressure with a clean cloth over a broad area to control blood loss, but do not apply pressure directly onto a suspected skull fracture. If blood soaks through, do not remove the original cloth. Instead, apply more cloths on top, and continue to apply pressure. If the person is vomiting, stabilize the head and neck, and carefully turn the victim to the side to prevent choking on vomit.",
+          "qualifier_or_exception": "All conditions and exceptions in this excerpt were checked against the complete card.",
+          "card_carries": true,
+          "verdict": "PASS"
+        },
+        {
+          "field_path": "do[4]",
+          "text": "لو بيرجّع، ثبّت راسه ورقبته ولفّه بالراحة على جنبه عشان مايشرقش في الترجيع.",
+          "source_id": "mlp:skull-fracture",
+          "source_context_section": "First Aid",
